merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-003\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a journey that would take about 4,5 years\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-004\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"its encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-005\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The Uranus encounter's geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-006\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-007\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"The first human-made object to fly past Uranus, Voyager 2's short-range observations of the planet began Jan. 31, 1986\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text identifies Voyager 2, not Voyager 1, as the first to fly past Uranus.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-008\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 2's short-range observations of the planet began Jan. 31, 1986\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text attributes this to Voyager 2 and dates it 1986, not Voyager 1 in 1987.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-009\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-010\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-011\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1986\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text states 1986, not 1968.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"A-012\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-001\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 2 discovered 10 new moons\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text states 10 new moons, not 11.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-002\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"given such names as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The names in the claim differ from the spellings given in the text.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-003\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"allusions to Shakespeare and Alexander Pope\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text attributes the names to Shakespeare and Pope, not Goethe.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-004\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"continuing a naming tradition begun in 1687\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-005\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"three new rings in addition to the “older” eight rings\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-006\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-007\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-008\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"450 km/h (450,000 meters per hour)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text equates 450 km/h to 450,000 meters per hour, not 72400.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-009\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-010\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"479 miles (900 kilometers)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-011\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-012\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The names in the claim (Ariele, Umbrella, Titan) do not match the text's Ariel, Umbriel, Titania.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-013\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"five of Uranus' smaller moons\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The moon names in the claim differ from those the text lists as the five smaller moons.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-014\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"flying by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-015\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-016\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text says nearly decade-long travels, not century-long.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-017\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Images of the moon showed a strange object whose surface was a mishmash of peculiar features\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-018\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-019\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The spectacular news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same day by the tragic Challenger accident\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Directly stated.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-020\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"the tragic Challenger accident that killed seven astronauts\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text says seven astronauts, not six.\"},\n{\"claim_id\":\"B-021\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"during their space shuttle launch Jan. 28, 1986\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text dates the launch Jan. 28, 1986, not Feb. 28, 1986.\"}\n]}","ttft_ms":10669,"type":"result","duration_ms":28751,"uuid":"c9d306fb-de69-4cfe-89d3-6dc0cd685584","ttft_stream_ms":3203,"time_to_request_ms":111,"first_content_frame_ms":3203,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
